# Build output — regenerated by do_build.bat every time, no reason to track.
build/
# QA-ModelShell TS6 (BLU-302): the 32-bit plugin-host helper's own build tree.
# Separate because an MSVC generator is single-platform per tree.
build32/

# Claude / planning working notes — local-only.
Files For Claude/

# User-created projects + their backups + samples — runtime data, not source.
Projects/

# Per-machine audio settings (different audio interfaces per workstation).
audio_settings.xml
# Transient sibling written by the Audio Settings dialog's Apply (consumed on
# restart to switch the device) — runtime, never source.
audio_settings_pending.xml
master_output.xml
# QA-ModelShell TS6: hosted-plugin scan folders + the user's added-plugin list,
# and JUCE's dead-man's-pedal crash list from scanning.  Per-machine runtime
# data (which plugins are INSTALLED here), never source.
plugins.xml
plugins_scan_crashes.txt

# Runtime diagnostic logs — regenerated each launch, not source.
*_log.txt
# JUCE's ASIO driver trace (JUCE_ASIO_DEBUGGING) — truncated and rewritten on
# every launch.  Not matched by *_log.txt above.
/asio_trace.txt

# QA-DispatcherAffinity trace dumps — one-shot diagnostic CSV captures from
# the (now-stripped) Mixer "QA-DispatcherAffinity Trace" menu item.  The
# feature that wrote them was removed at the QA-DispatcherAffinity Task 4
# strip; this pattern is belt-and-suspenders so any stray captures (or a
# future re-run of an equivalent trace) never get swept into a commit.
qa-dispatcheraffinity-trace*.log

# Auto-saved Untitled-project backups — runtime, not source.
Backups/Unsaved/

# Undo-history structural snapshots (UndoSnapshotStore) — one XML per structural
# op, written to the app root at runtime and pruned when the undo manager drops
# the transaction. Same class as Backups/Unsaved/; was never listed.
UndoSnapshots/

# Manuals packaged for sending to someone. Regenerable from Manuals/ in one
# command, so it is an output rather than a source — same reasoning as build/.
/BaySickDAW-Manuals.zip

# The three printable manuals (one per depth level) — printed from
# Manuals/manual.html by headless Edge, ~30 MB of regenerable binary that
# would churn on every manual edit. The installer picks them up from the
# staged Manuals/ folder; they are outputs, not source.
/Manuals/*.pdf
/Manuals/shots-staging/

# Per-machine general settings (recent files, multi-core toggle, etc.) — modified every app launch.
settings.xml

# Python bytecode caches (Claude skill scripts).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS metadata files.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db

# Editor backups + temp.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.bak
*.orig

# Windows shortcuts — per-machine paths.
*.lnk

# Build / debug output at repo root (broader than the *_log.txt rule).
/build_*.txt
/configure_*.txt
/startup_*.txt
/freeze_timing.txt

# Personal sample imports (mirrors the Presets/.../My Presets/ rule).
My Samples/

# Claude agent worktrees — created by isolated-mode subagents; ephemeral, not source.
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-machine Claude Code permission grants — local-only by Claude convention (`*.local.*`).
# Backups included: the file is gitignored, so a prune has no other undo path, and the
# backups hold superseded grants that must never re-enter history.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.bak-*

# User-created presets across every page / engine / effect — personal content, not stock.
# Stock factory presets live alongside (e.g. "Presets/Effects/Reverb/Hall.xml"); only the
# "My Presets" subfolders contain user-saved patches that shouldn't ship in the repo.
Presets/**/My Presets/

# User-created project templates — personal content, not stock.  Mirrors the
# Presets/.../My Presets/ rule for the Templates/ folder.
Templates/My Templates/

# User-saved drum kits — personal content, not stock.  Mirrors the My Presets
# rule; the rule was missing when the Kits/ tree first landed, so one user kit
# was tracked until 2026-08-16.
Kits/My Kits/

# Local-only planning notes from earlier in the project (when it was still
# called Vibesynth). Personal scratch, not part of the public source.
SaturdayNightMasacre.md

# Jeff's personal issue-tracker log inside the Plans & Specs/ tree — a local
# scratch file where he jots items to relay to Claude.  Local-only, not source.
Plans & Specs/Issue Tracker.txt

# Stub JUCE-generated key-mapping XML at repo root. The 3 mappings in this
# file are NOT the app's real keybinds (those live in KeyBindsWindow.cpp);
# this is a leftover JUCE auto-generated artefact that escaped earlier
# cleanup. Per-machine and not source.
/keymap.xml

# QA-Fe pitch-engine A/B render byproducts (2026-07-13) — throwaway comparison
# QA-Fe2 (2026-07-16): per-machine UI prefs (File Settings checkboxes etc.) --
# sibling of settings.xml, never shipped.
/ui_prefs.xml

# clips from the WORLD/Signalsmith/Rubber Band engine evaluation, not shipped.
/SIM_*.wav
/PV_*.wav
/RBLIVE_*.wav
/RUBBERBAND_*.wav
/SIGSMITH_*.wav
/WORLD_*.wav
/enable_pitch_diag.txt

# QA-OctavePedal octave-engine A/B render byproducts (2026-07-18) — throwaway
# old-vs-new dev comparison clips for the pitch-synchronous octave-down rework;
# regenerable from the scratchpad A/B script, never shipped.
/octave_ab_*.wav

# QA-Fe pitch-engine test harnesses (2026-07-13) — throwaway build/render
# scaffolding for the engine A/B; stripped at QA-Fe Task 7.
/Tools/signalsmith-test/
/Tools/rubberband-test/
/Tools/pitch-sim/

# QA-Fe garble investigation dumps (2026-07-15) -- verbatim pipeline map +
# adversarial-verification notes generated for external review; analysis
# artifacts, not shipped source.
/PITCH_PIPELINE_BREAKDOWN.md
/PITCH_PIPELINE_VERIFICATION.md

# QA-G3Smoke crash-hunt artifacts (2026-07-24) -- do_build.bat archives each
# outgoing Release exe+pdb pair (dump symbolization); WER LocalDumps writes
# crash .dmp files here.  Both are per-machine runtime data, never source.
/SymbolStore/
/CrashDumps/

# KBS DAW fork (2026-09-02) - the shell fork's own git repository, seeded into
# this tree per "Plans & Specs/KBS DAW Fork - Design.md" section 9.1.  It moves
# to the KBS side with its history; never tracked here.
KBS DAW/
